hey everyone it's sarah with  registerednessrn.com and in this video  i'm going to demonstrate how to recap a  needle using the one hand  scoop technique now you want to avoid  recapping needles  due to the high risk of needle stick  injuries  however sometimes as a nurse you have to  recap a needle  and to do this safely you want to use a  technique that decreases the risk of a  needle stick  when recapping a needle you want to  avoid using this technique as it carries  a much greater risk for a needle stick  injury therefore it is recommended that  when you  do have to recap a needle that you use  the one hand scoop technique  so i have a situation where i need to  recap this needle  because i have used this needle to  withdraw medication from a vial  and i need to remove this needle and  apply a new one  so i can administer it to the patient so  i have kept the original cap and  packaging to help assist me do this  so what i'm going to do is  i'm going to use just one hand hence why  we call it the one  hand scoop technique i'm going to keep  my non-dominant hand by my side so i'm  only going to have my dominant hand  holding the barrel of the syringe and  then carefully  i'm going to place the needle  inside of the cap until i can no longer  get it inside the cap  then i'm going to lift up like this  and then take that one hand that i  wasn't using and just snap the cap on  alternatively when using the one hand  scoop technique  some protocols require that you use a  hard surface to snap the cap into place  without using the other hand then i'm  going to remove and dispose of the  needle per my facilities protocol  okay so that wraps up this demonstration  on how to recap a needle using the one  hand scoop technique  and if you'd like to watch some other  nursing skill videos you can access the  link in the youtube description below
 

